{
  "index": 8,
  "response": " Here is an implementation of Bubble Sort in Python for sorting an array `a` of 500 strings:\n\n```python\ndef bubble_sort(a):\n    n = len(a)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        swapped = False\n        for j in range(0, n-i-1):\n            if a[j] > a[j+1]:\n                a[j], a[j+1] = a[j+1], a[j]\n                swapped = True\n        if not swapped:\n            break\n\na = [\"string\" * random.randint(1, 10) for _ in range(500)]  # Generate array of strings\nrandom.shuffle(a)  # Unorganized array\nbubble_sort(a)     # Sort using bubble sort\n```\n\nThis code first generates an array of 500 random strings and then sorts it using the Bubble Sort algorithm. The array is initialized with strings that are `\"string\"` repeated between 1 to 10 times, so you can replace it with your own string objects if needed.",
